      {
        "number": 8,
        "internalPageId": null,
        "title": "Statements Questions Answers 1 You should talk to her. Should I talk to her? Yes, you should talk to her. 2 We have to be nice to them. Do you have to be nice to them? No, we don’t have to be nice to them. 3 She must be careful now. Must she be careful now? No, she mustn't be careful now. 4 They can’t act like children. Can they act like children? Yes, they can act like children.",
        "visibleTexts": [
          "Statements Questions Answers 1 You should talk to her. Should I talk to her? Yes, you should talk to her. 2 We have to be nice to them. Do you have to be nice to them? No, we don’t have to be nice to them. 3 She must be careful now. Must she be careful now? No, she mustn't be careful now. 4 They can’t act like children. Can they act like children? Yes, they can act like children.",
          "We can talk about people’s behaviour and how they are supposed to act by using modals.",
          "To consider 1. All verbs go in simple form after a modal. 2. Modals work with all pronouns with no problem. 3. Modals affect the main verbs according to the speaker's intention. 4. Would is also a common modal; You’ll hear more of it in an upcoming lesson."
        ],
